# Git Branch Workflow

**Target repo:** https://github.com/asheeshsahu/HybridFitApp.git (upstream)  
**Do NOT use** asheesh-sahuSFDC (origin) for new branches.

## 1. Create a child branch from upstream/main

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout -b <branch-name> upstream/main
```

Use a descriptive branch name (e.g., `feature/hydration-fix`, `fix/meal-tracking`).

## 2. Make changes

Implement the requested changes on the new branch only.

## 3. Commit and push to asheeshsahu (upstream)

```bash
git add <changed-files>
git commit -m "<descriptive message>"
git push -u upstream <branch-name>
```

Or with token auth:
```bash
git push -u https://<token>@github.com/asheeshsahu/HybridFitApp.git <branch-name>
```

## 4. Sync

After pushing, ensure upstream is in sync. Fetch and rebase if needed:
```bash
git fetch upstream
git rebase upstream/main  # if working on a branch
```

## Rules

- **Always** branch from `upstream/main` (asheeshsahu/HybridFitApp)
- **Always** push to `upstream` (asheeshsahu), not origin (asheesh-sahuSFDC)
- **Never** commit directly to main
